    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d198-a1">

                <pb facs="0192" n="118" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg118"/>

                <head>Viscount Monck to Mr. Burnley</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Quebec,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-03-28"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 28, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your despatch of the 22d instant, and its enclosures, containing information
                    given by Mr. ——, of ——, Canada West, relative to alleged projected raids from
                    Canada into the United States.</p>
                <p>In reply, I have the honor to state that the information contained in Mr. ——‘s
                    letters had already been communicated to the Canadian government, and that a
                    special agent had been sent to Ampréor to investigate the truth of his
                    statements.</p>
                <p>I have not yet received his report, but I shall not fail to communicate it to you
                    should any grounds appear to exist for attaching credit to Mr. ——‘s
                    allegations.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>MONCK.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>J. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hume Burnley,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
